9,Beami language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/beami_language,"Beami (also known as Bedamuni, Bedamini, or Mougulu) is a Papuan language belonging to the Bosavi branch of the Trans-New Guinea family, spoken primarily by around 5,000 people in the Western Province (east of Nomad) and Southern Highlands Province of Papua New Guinea.",Bedamuni,Trans-New Guinea
